  "constraints": "* Input arrays/tensors are non-empty and well-formed\n* Floating point values are finite real numbers\n* Numerical operations must adhere to standard precision tolerances",
  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_zero_pad_and_center_crop(image: list, pad: int, crop_h: int, crop_w: int) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Zero Pad and Center Crop** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_zero_pad_and_center_crop(image: list, pad: int, crop_h: int, crop_w: int) -> list:\n    img, p = np.array(image, dtype=np.float64), int(pad)\n    padded = np.pad(img, ((p, p), (p, p)), mode='constant')\n    sh, sw = (padded.shape[0] - int(crop_h)) // 2, (padded.shape[1] - int(crop_w)) // 2\n    return np.round(padded[sh:sh+int(crop_h), sw:sw+int(crop_w)], 6).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
